# Mutations for the ACC=0 arm of rtl/amx_fp8.v. Run with:
#   scripts/mutate.sh -r rtl/amx_fp8.v -t tb/tb_amx_fp8.v -m tb/mut/amx_fp8_acc0.mut \
#       -P "-Ptb_amx_fp8.ACC=0" \
#       -x rtl/fp8_mul.v -x rtl/fp32_add.v -x rtl/fx2fp32.v -x rtl/maxmag64.v
#
#=========================================================== WHY THIS EXISTS
# X2's one inviolable condition is that ACC=0 stays bit-identical to row p1. The
# 28 passing cases and the four golden constants show that the CURRENT bytes are
# right; they say nothing about whether the tests would still NOTICE if the
# parameterisation had quietly broken the conformant path.
#
# That is not a hypothetical. Introducing ACC moved the p1 datapath inside an
# `if (ACC == 0)` generate arm and moved the cacc flop block outside it, driven
# through two new wires. Either change could have gone wrong in a way that a
# passing test suite would hide if the suite had no teeth on the p1 arm.
#
# So these mutations attack the ACC=0 path specifically, including the shared
# plumbing the fork created.

#-------------------------------------------------- the epilogue schedule (p1)
# The lane combine order. tb/fp8_golden.py measures that a balanced tree and a
# sequential chain disagree on ~23% of elements, so these must be caught.
EP0 pairs 0+2 and 1+3          ||| s/                        assign opb = ep0 \? lacc\[1\*ACC_W \+: ACC_W\]/                        assign opb = ep0 ? lacc[2*ACC_W +: ACC_W]/
EP1 combines the wrong lane    ||| s/                                   : ep1 \? lacc\[2\*ACC_W \+: ACC_W\]/                                   : ep1 ? lacc[1*ACC_W +: ACC_W]/
lane 2 never pairs with lane 3 ||| s/                        assign opb = ep0 \? lacc\[3\*ACC_W \+: ACC_W\]\n                                         : prod\[2\*ACC_W \+: ACC_W\];/                        assign opb = prod[2*ACC_W +: ACC_W];/
EP2 adds C to the wrong lane   ||| s/                                   : ep2 \? cacc\[gm\]\[gn\]/                                   : ep2 ? lacc[3*ACC_W +: ACC_W]/
lane 0 loses its EP1 enable    ||| s/                        assign len\[gb\] = acc_phase \| ep0 \| ep1;/                        assign len[gb] = acc_phase | ep0;/
lane 2 loses its EP0 enable    ||| s/                        assign len\[gb\] = acc_phase \| ep0;/                        assign len[gb] = acc_phase;/
accumulate one cycle short     ||| s/    wire       acc_phase = run && \(ccnt < KDW\[CW-1:0\]\);/    wire       acc_phase = run \&\& (ccnt < KDW[CW-1:0] - 1);/
instruction ends one cycle early ||| s/    localparam integer LASTC = \(ACC == 0\) \? EP2 : EP1;/    localparam integer LASTC = (ACC == 0) ? EP1 : EP1;/

#----------------------------------------------- the lane accumulators (p1)
lanes not cleared at start     ||| s/                    if \(lane_clr\)    lacc\[0\*ACC_W \+: ACC_W\] <= \{ACC_W\{1.b0\}\};/                    if (1'b0)        lacc[0*ACC_W +: ACC_W] <= {ACC_W{1'b0}};/
lane 1 fed lane 0's product    ||| s/                    end else begin : g_opb_plain\n                        assign opb = prod\[gb\*ACC_W \+: ACC_W\];/                    end else begin : g_opb_plain\n                        assign opb = prod[0*ACC_W +: ACC_W];/
# SURVIVES, and correctly. fp32_add is commutative -- tb_fp32_add.v asserts it on
# every one of its 121k vectors, and the unit does an internal magnitude swap so
# both ports are symmetric in delay as well as in value. Which port carries the
# loop is therefore a DOCUMENTATION choice, not a correctness one: rtl/amx_fp8.v
# says "operand A is always lacc[gb], straight out of the flop", and that sentence
# describes intent rather than a constraint the tests could enforce. Recorded so a
# reader does not go looking for the missing test.
=adder operands swapped        ||| s/                        .a \(lacc\[gb\*ACC_W \+: ACC_W\]\),\n                        .b \(opb\),/                        .a (opb),\n                        .b (lacc[gb*ACC_W +: ACC_W]),/

#---------------------------------------- the plumbing the ACC fork created
# c_next / c_wr are new wires that both arms drive and one flop block consumes.
# If the fork had crossed them, ACC=0 would write C from the wrong place.
C written from lane 1 not 0    ||| s/                assign c_next = sum\[0\*ACC_W \+: ACC_W\];/                assign c_next = sum[1*ACC_W +: ACC_W];/
C write enable stuck on        ||| s/                assign c_wr   = ep2;/                assign c_wr   = 1'b1;/
C write enable never fires     ||| s/                assign c_wr   = ep2;/                assign c_wr   = 1'b0;/
C tile load loses its row test ||| s/                    if \(tile_we && tile_sel == SEL_C && tile_row == gm\)/                    if (tile_we \&\& tile_sel == SEL_C)/
C tile load beats nothing      ||| s/                    else if \(c_wr\)\n                        cacc\[gm\]\[gn\] <= c_next;/                    else if (1'b0)\n                        cacc[gm][gn] <= c_next;/

#-------------------------------------------------- operand delivery, shared
# Common to both arms, so a break here is a break in the thing that makes the
# ACC=0 vs ACC=1 comparison controlled.
A dword index ignores k        ||| s/            assign a_dw_all\[gm\*32 \+: 32\] = a_flat\[gm\*512 \+ kcnt\*32 \+: 32\];/            assign a_dw_all[gm*32 +: 32] = a_flat[gm*512 +: 32];/
B row index ignores k          ||| s/    wire \[511:0\]        b_row = b_flat\[kcnt\*512 \+: 512\];/    wire [511:0]        b_row = b_flat[0 +: 512];/
A decoded with B's format      ||| s/    wire fmt_a = op_r\[1\];        \/\/ 1 = HF8\/E4M3/    wire fmt_a = op_r[0];/
op read live instead of latched ||| s/    wire fmt_a = op_r\[1\];        \/\/ 1 = HF8\/E4M3/    wire fmt_a = op[1];/

#---------------------------------------------------------- proven equivalent
# Lanes 1 and 3 are DEAD from EP0 onward: EP0 consumes them combinationally on the
# same edge that overwrites lanes 0 and 2, and nothing reads them again. So
# widening their enable is unobservable. This was established by mutation during
# the p1 build and is recorded in rtl/amx_fp8.v's comments; keeping it here means
# the claim is re-checked rather than merely asserted.
=lanes 1 and 3 enabled in EP0  ||| s/                    end else begin : g_en_plain\n                        assign len\[gb\] = acc_phase;/                    end else begin : g_en_plain\n                        assign len[gb] = acc_phase | ep0;/
